# Linear fit to synthetic data

## Dataset

40 synthetic points generated with NumPy, legacy `RandomState(0)`:

```python
x = np.linspace(0, 10, 40)
rng = np.random.RandomState(0)
y = 2*x + 1 + rng.normal(0, 0.5, 40)
```

True line y = 2x + 1 with additive Gaussian noise of standard deviation 0.5.

## Method

Ordinary least squares regression of y on a constant and x. Two-sided 95% confidence intervals for slope and intercept from the Student-t distribution with df = n − 2 = 38, using the residual-variance estimate σ̂² = RSS/38 and its standard errors. Code and exact data/fit are kept in the experiment-repo repository as provenance (files `analysis/fit_line.py` and `analysis/fit_results.json` in world/experiment-repo; they are not part of the final assembled report).

## Results

| Parameter | Estimate | SE | 95% CI |
|---|---|---|---|
| Intercept | 1.3987 | 0.1632 | [1.0683, 1.7290] |
| Slope | 1.9515 | 0.0281 | [1.8947, 2.0084] |

Residual SD σ̂ = 0.5258 (σ̂² = 0.2764). The true slope 2 falls inside its 95% interval; the true intercept 1 falls outside its interval [1.0683, 1.7290], which can occur by chance at the 5% level.

